---
title: "What rises, what drowns on Hacker News"
date: 2026-07-24
author: Nikolay Bryskin
description: "Every story submitted to Hacker News over 60 days — 59,711 of them — cut by topic, format, source, timing, and title shape: what reaches the front page and what dies on /newest."
image: /uploads/hn-what-rises-what-drowns/cover.png
tags:
  - hackernews
  - data
  - blogging
layout:
readingInfo:
  minutes: 8
  words: 1600
feedContent: |
  <p>Every story submitted to Hacker News over the last 60 days — 59,711 of them — pulled from the Algolia API and cut by topic, format, source, timing, and title shape. 40.7% drown at 1–2 points and only 4.4% reach 100+ — but the odds swing 10× with choices you control: personal blogs own three-quarters of the front page, AI is the most oversupplied and worst-converting topic, question-mark titles sink, and the single best posting window is Saturday evening US.</p>
  <p><a href="https://zxczxc.dev/posts/hn-what-rises-what-drowns/">Open the interactive edition</a></p>
